WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.789
Donald Trump did not go to Joe Biden's inauguration
breaking with tradition.

00:00:06.789 --> 00:00:13.510
The first president in, I believe, 152 years
not to go to their replacement's inauguration.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:14.650
Trump left.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:20.750
He went to Florida early this morning, but
on his way out, he did leave the White House

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.460
and take the Marine One helicopter to Andrews
Air Force Base.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.920
And before getting on Air Force One for that
final flight, delivered a five or seven minute

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.730
speech and said even more things that make
no sense to a very deflated crowd.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.780
Trump asking to be remembered if things improve
under Biden.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.540
Trump saying if things do get better in the
next few months, it's because of me.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.820
Please remember me.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.320
You're going to see incredible numbers start
coming in.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:52.449
If everything is sort of left alone, be careful,
very complex, be careful.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:56.820
But you're going to see some incredible things
happening.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:04.000
And remember us when you see these things
happening of you would remember us because

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.530
I'm looking at I'm looking at elements of
our economy that are set to be a rocket ship.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.000
It's a rocket ship.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.430
Very powerful elements of the economy that
he's looking at, as he says there, how long

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.320
overdue is it for this nightmare to be over?

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:26.690
This morning's speech really reminded me of
that Trump still using the term China virus.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:31.080
Another aspect of how this morning's speech
was almost the same as the campaign speeches

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.700
Trump had been giving China virus.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.120
It's a horrible thing that was put onto the
world.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.950
We all know where it came from, but it's a
horrible, horrible thing.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:43.950
So be very careful.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.780
Be very, very careful.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:52.070
But we want to pay great love, great love
to all of the people that have suffered, including

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.060
families who have suffered so gravely.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:01.320
And then that's really the first time I've
heard Trump sincere, sort of sincerely mention

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.500
the people who have actually suffered from
the virus.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.720
Trump for good measure.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.950
He can't get away from these things again,
claiming the 1918 flu started in 1917.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.720
We don't know why he's been saying this for
a year, but he said it again, put it in a

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:25.860
position like it's never been before, despite
the worst plague to hit since, I guess you'd

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.640
say, 1917 over a hundred years ago.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:37.150
And it is a good bye for now as Donald Trump
pledges to be back and says have a nice life

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.840
to the crowd, sort of the sendoff we would
expect from the guy who never really cared

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.810
about his supporters as people.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:49.320
He cared about them only in so far as it was
useful to his political goals.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.900
The things that we've done have been just
incredible.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.120
And I couldn't have done them, done it without
you.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.700
So just a goodbye.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.240
We love you.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:12.600
We will be back in some form.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:18.600
And again, I want to just living I want to
thank our vice president, Mike Pence and Karen,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:23.319
I want to thank Congress because we really
worked well with Congress, at least certain

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:26.260
elements of Congress, but we really did.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.470
We've gotten so much done that nobody thought
would be possible.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.510
What I do want to thank Congress and I want
to thank all of the great people of Washington,

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.630
D.C., all of the people that we worked with
to put this miracle together.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.240
So have a good life.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.760
We will see you soon.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.760
Thank you.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.990
Thank you very much.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:50.390
Thank you very much.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.590
So there it is.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:58.069
Have a nice life and you hear YMCA cranking
up there, a surreal and bizarre moment.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:04.480
And with that, Donald Trump is done flying
off into the sunrise, not into the sunset.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.510
It was early this morning, flying off tomorrow.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:12.380
Lago in Palm Beach, Florida, before Joe Biden's
inauguration, alluding to, we don't know if

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.740
it's a twenty, twenty four run, although I
don't expect that.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:19.190
We don't know if it's alluding to there were
rumors of Trump starting a new party to be

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.220
different than the Republican Party.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:25.570
Rumors of many different things we just don't
know.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:30.830
But hours before leaving office, Donald Trump
issuing one hundred and forty three pardons.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:05:42.430
And I do want to talk about that.

